The function's work is dominated by the `GetField(18)` scan and the validity check, so I only collapsed the null-check into a single short-circuit expression, letting the compiler keep the fast path branchless and avoiding the extra early-return block; behavior is identical.
```cpp
    FIT_BOOL IsMaxCadenceValid() const
    {
        const Field* field = GetField(18);
        return (FIT_NULL != field) && field->IsValueValid();
    }

```